    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0556" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg472"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-02-03"><hi rendition="#italic">February 3,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. White reports that he has just seen copies of sundry telegrams recently
                    exchanged between Lord Lansdowne and the British ambassador at Washington. The
                    latest British proposal is that the 30 per cent of customs of the two ports,
                    estimated at £213,861, be added to the 13 per cent of entire Venezuelan customs
                    receipts, estimated at £61,782, making a total of £275,643, of which one-half be
                    taken by the three allied powers and the other half by all other powers having
                    claims against Venezuela. If Mr. Bowen refuses assent the British <pb
                        facs="0557" n="473" xml:id="pg473"/> ambassador is instructed to propose the
                    signature of a protocol embodying all the points agreed upon, and reference of
                    priority of claims question to The Hague, unless the President of the United
                    States will pass upon it.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
